      "released_evidence_ids": [],
      "reply": "That makes sense: a new title can feel awkward because saying it out loud makes the change feel public and real, while “designer” still names the part of your work that feels familiar. You don’t have to erase that identity to name the role you’re growing into.\n\nYou could try an introduction that holds both:\n\n> “Hi, I’m [name]. I’m a designer by background, and I’m now managing the team. I’m enjoying learning how to support the work from a different angle.”\n\nOr, more simply:\n\n> “I’m [name], the team manager. I came from design, so I still think like a designer while I’m learning this role.”\n\nThe goal isn’t to sound perfectly settled. It’s to use words that are true now and leave room for the identity to become more familiar.",
